# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reachy Mini Agent — environment variables
# Production: copy to /home/pollen/brain/.env on Pi (loaded by the systemd
#   user unit via `EnvironmentFile=`; see systemd/robot-brain.service.example).
# Dev: copy to `.env`, then `set -a; source .env; set +a` before running the
#   brain manually (e.g. `python -m robot_brain`).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Reachy connection ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Host/IP of the Reachy Mini daemon. Use mDNS name by default; set to a
# specific IP (LAN or Tailscale) for remote control.
REACHY_HOST=reachy-mini.local

# Opt-in monkey-patch for SDK 1.7.x wireless MediaManager.signalling_host bug
# (see commit 7f7f85d). REQUIRED only when robot-brain runs on a SEPARATE
# compute box reaching the robot over Tailscale/another LAN — the SDK then
# mis-derives signalling_host from daemon's wlan_ip and WebRTC times out.
# When brain runs co-located on the Pi itself, leave UNSET: the SDK
# auto-detects localhost correctly and the patch would actively misroute.
# Accepted "on" values: any non-empty string EXCEPT 0/false/no/off (case
# insensitive). e.g. REACHY_MEDIA_REMOTE=1 enables; =0 leaves it off.
# REACHY_MEDIA_REMOTE=1

# ── LLM (brain) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LLM_MODE is informational only as of 2026-06-01 — the multi-provider
# failover chain (litellm / anthropic / claude-cli) was removed after a
# year on vLLM with zero invocations in production logs (see ADR-0005).
# Single-path dispatch now goes through _ask_via_ollama, which switches
# transport based on LLM_BACKEND.
LLM_MODE=vllm

# Backend for the actual chat HTTP call. vllm (default) dispatches to a
# vLLM /v1/chat/completions endpoint (continuous batching, concurrent
# vision+dialog, AWQ-Marlin). ollama keeps the legacy local-Ollama path
# available for dev boxes that don't have vLLM running.
LLM_BACKEND=vllm               # vllm | ollama

# vLLM endpoint (only used when LLM_BACKEND=vllm). VLLM_HOST accepts a bare
# host (preferred new convention) OR a full URL (legacy). When bare-host form
# is used, VLLM_PORT is appended as http://{host}:{port}. enable_thinking is
# OFF by default on every chat call (chat_template_kwargs) — qwen3.6 thinking
# mode + tight max_tokens truncates <tool_call> to empty content (see
# project_synth_e2e_bench_2026_05_13).
VLLM_HOST=vllm0528             # primary; Tailscale MagicDNS
VLLM_PORT=8000
VLLM_MODEL=qwen36-awq          # served-model-name from vllm serve
# VLLM_HOST_BACKUP removed 2026-06-01 (Track D-2). Never wired to inline retry
# — pybreaker + tenacity in brain_observability handle backend resilience.
# Manual failover: just `export VLLM_HOST=<backup> && systemctl --user restart reachy-brain`.

# vLLM serve script speculative-decoding knobs.
# WARNING — backend-specific defaults:
#   * 2× RTX 3090 (s1, scripts/vllm_serve.sh): MTP_K=3 + prefix-cache OFF
#     was the v4.0 winner. See https://github.com/thc1006/qwen3.6-vllm-2x3090/releases/tag/v4.0
#   * 2× V100 SM 7.0 (vllm0528, scripts/vllm_serve_v100.sh): leave MTP_K=0.
#     2026-05-28 empirical: k=2/3/4 acceptance ~0% on 1Cat-vLLM v1.0.0,
#     speedup 1.2× = noise. The serve script does NOT pass --speculative-config.
# MTP_K=0                       # 0=off; 1=v3 canonical; 2=pre-v4; 3=v4 winner (3090 only)
# ENABLE_PREFIX_CACHING=0       # off when MTP on (vllm-project/vllm#38182)

# Ollama (local)
OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434
OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen3.6:35b-a3b
OLLAMA_THINK=0                 # 1 = chain-of-thought mode (slower)

# LLM runtime behaviour
LLM_STREAMING=1                # 1 = stream TTS sentence-by-sentence (lower latency)
LLM_TOOLS=1                    # 1 = expose robot_tools to Ollama tool-call loop
LLM_TOOL_MAX_ITERS=3           # cap on tool_call → result → LLM round-trips per turn

# Long-term memory (Mem0 + embedded Qdrant; LLM via Ollama OR vLLM, embed via Ollama OR FastEmbed)
ROBOT_MEMORY=1                 # 1 = enable Mem0 fact extraction + rolling summary
MEM0_USER_ID=default           # partitions Qdrant by user for multi-person setups
MEM0_NAMESPACE=elder_facts     # metadata tag attached to every add() — partitions by domain
# Provider selection (env-driven). Defaults stay backward-compatible (ollama+ollama).
# On the Pi we use openai+fastembed because Ollama is not installed; vLLM serves LLM
# fact extraction and FastEmbed does CPU embeddings.
MEM0_LLM_PROVIDER=ollama       # ollama | openai (use "openai" to point at vLLM)
MEM0_EMBED_PROVIDER=ollama     # ollama | fastembed (CPU-only ONNX, no torch)
MEM0_LLM_MODEL=qwen3.6:35b-a3b # ollama: tag name; openai: vLLM served-model-name
MEM0_EMBED_MODEL=bge-m3        # ollama: tag; fastembed: HF id (e.g. BAAI/bge-small-zh-v1.5)
MEM0_EMBED_DIMS=1024           # bge-m3=1024; BAAI/bge-small-zh-v1.5=512; MUST match model
# Used only when MEM0_LLM_PROVIDER=openai
MEM0_LLM_BASE_URL=http://vllm0528:8000/v1
MEM0_LLM_API_KEY=dummy         # vLLM ignores the value but openai client requires one
# Optional overrides (defaults: ~/dev/reachy-agent/robot/.qdrant_memory + conversation_summary.txt)
# WARNING: SD card wear — Qdrant does mmap+segment compaction; consider tmpfs
# or USB SSD for long-term deployments. Setting MEM0_QDRANT_PATH to a path
# under /home/pollen/ or $HOME triggers a runtime startup warning.
# MEM0_QDRANT_PATH=/home/pollen/brain/.qdrant_memory
# MEM0_SUMMARY_PATH=/home/pollen/brain/conversation_summary.txt
# conversation_log.jsonl is append-only without fsync; last few turns may be
# lost on SIGKILL. Acceptable for elder-care dialog (next turn re-establishes
# context) but do not treat the log as a system-of-record audit trail.

# ── Vision (VLM) — periodic scene description for LLM prompt ──────────
# Option A (current): dedicated Moondream2 wrapper on vllm0528 card 1, isolated
# from the qwen36-awq engine on card 0. Speaks OpenAI /v1/chat/completions and
# Ollama /api/chat. ~0.4-1.2s per query, FP16 ~4-5 GiB.
VISION_URL=http://vllm0528:8002        # Moondream2 OpenAI-compat wrapper (card 1)
VISION_MODEL=moondream2                # name is informational; backend ignores it
VISION_INTERVAL=10                     # seconds between frame captures

# ── STT (Whisper) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
WHISPER_URL=http://vllm0528:9000
STT_DUMP=0                              # 1 = save every captured WAV to /tmp/stt_dump/ (debug)
# When WHISPER_URL is set, brain skips local faster_whisper init by default
# (saves ~25s startup + CUDA VRAM). Set PREFER_LOCAL_WHISPER=1 to keep a local
# Whisper warm anyway — only useful on hosts that have faster_whisper installed
# AND want a local fallback for remote outages.
# PREFER_LOCAL_WHISPER=0

# ── Elder-care features (P6/P7/P8) ────────────────────────────────────
# All gated behind ELDER_CARE_MODE. Off by default — non-elder deploys see
# zero behavior change. When on:
#   P6 = emergency-phrase pre-LLM webhook route
#   P7 = TTS rate -10% + post-TTS pause +ELDER_PAUSE_MS
#   P8 = antenna visual "listening" cue on VAD rising edge
# ELDER_CARE_MODE=1
# ELDER_EMERGENCY_WEBHOOK_URL=https://your-webhook.example/elder-alert
# ELDER_EMERGENCY_LOG_PATH=/home/pollen/brain/logs/emergency.log
# ELDER_PAUSE_MS=400
# ELDER_ANTENNA_DIP_RAD=0.15

# ── Cascaded perception (opt-in YOLO Tier-1) ──────────────────────────
# Always-on cheap object detector that gives the LLM a fresh object list
# without invoking the heavy multimodal VL on every frame. Requires
# ultralytics in the venv.
VISION_CASCADE=0                        # 1 = start the YOLO cascade thread
CASCADE_MODEL=yolov8n.pt                # ultralytics model name or local path
CASCADE_INTERVAL=0.5                    # seconds between detections (2 Hz default)
CASCADE_CONF=0.35                       # confidence threshold
CASCADE_TOPK=8                          # max distinct object names per frame
CASCADE_VERBOSE=0                       # 1 = print every detection list

# ── TTS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CANONICAL ROUTING KNOB (since ADR-0009-tts-routing, 2026-06-01).
# TTS_BACKEND is the ONLY knob production should set. Values:
#   edge                = Microsoft Azure cloud (needs internet); falls back to kokoro.
#   kokoro              = Local GPU (kokoro-onnx, kokoro_server.py); falls back to edge.
#   cosyvoice           = Self-hosted CosyVoice 2 on vllm0528 card 0;
#                         falls back to edge.
#   edge_then_cosyvoice = Try edge first, fall back to cosyvoice on Azure outage.
# When TTS_BACKEND is set, _stream_tts dispatches on it and never reads
# TTS_ENGINE. Production sits on TTS_BACKEND=edge.
TTS_BACKEND=edge

# DEPRECATED — use TTS_BACKEND instead. Setting both is undefined behaviour;
# TTS_BACKEND wins. Brain logs a one-shot `tts_engine_deprecated` warning at
# startup when this env is set, regardless of value. Keep commented out in
# production. Legacy values were edge | kokoro | hagen (HaGen kept routable
# via the legacy switch for operator muscle memory during the deprecation
# window).
# TTS_ENGINE=edge

KOKORO_URL=http://localhost:8880
KOKORO_VOICE=af_heart                   # af_heart / af_nicole / af_sky / af_bella ...

# CosyVoice 2 self-host (TTS_BACKEND=cosyvoice). vllm0528 card 0, fp16,
# 24 kHz output. Multilingual zh/en/ja/ko. Brain side circuit-breaker uses
# fail_max=2 (override in brain_observability._BACKEND_FAIL_MAX) so a vllm0528
# outage trips the breaker quickly and edge-tts takes over within ~16 s.
COSYVOICE_URL=http://vllm0528:8881
COSYVOICE_TIMEOUT_S=8                   # per-request HTTP timeout, seconds

# HaGen v4 (TTS_ENGINE=hagen) — GPT-SoVITS server settings
HAGEN_TTS_URL=http://100.124.198.14:8011/tts   # 5090 Tailscale IP, FastAPI port 8011
HAGEN_TTS_TIMEOUT_S=20                  # HTTP request timeout (seconds)
HAGEN_MIN_LEN=12                        # raw text < N chars → bypass HaGen, use Edge
                                        # (HaGen unreliable on short/intro utterances)

# TTS audio shaping
TTS_PEAK=0.95                           # peak-normalize each utterance to this level
TTS_GAIN=1.0                            # multiplied after normalization; >1 will clip
TTS_TAIL_DRAIN_S=0.4                    # post-TTS mic-gate hold time (USB+WebRTC drain)
TTS_VOICE=                              # Lock Edge TTS to a single voice for ALL languages
                                        # (e.g. zh-TW-HsiaoYuNeural reads English with a
                                        # Chinese accent — "Google 小姐" style — instead of
                                        # voice-switching mid-conversation). Empty = auto.

# TTS cache
TTS_CACHE_DIR=                           # default: <repo>/tts_cache
TTS_CACHE_MAX_MB=50                     # LRU eviction threshold

# ── Motor safety / observability ──────────────────────────────────────
# Face tracker delta clamp: max degrees per frame the absolute-pose
# set_target may move. At 30 FPS, 1.5° = 45°/sec ceiling. Values are
# clamped to [0.1°, 45°]; NaN / non-numeric / out-of-range fall back to 1.5.
FACE_TRACK_MAX_DELTA_DEG=1.5

# Face tracker absolute hard cap: head_pitch/yaw can never be commanded
# outside ±N degrees from neutral, regardless of delta-clamp baseline
# state. Backs up the delta clamp on bug paths (wrong baseline state,
# unit confusion). Tracker normally outputs [-20, +25]°, so 30° is
# comfortably permissive. Values clamped to [1°, 60°]; NaN / non-numeric
# fall back to 30.
FACE_TRACK_MAX_ABS_DEG=30

# Minimum LLM-issued move_head duration (seconds). Even if the LLM passes
# duration=0, the daemon goto call is clamped to this lower bound to prevent
# instant motor motion.
MOTOR_MIN_DURATION_S=1.8

# JSONL motor command log path. Records every set_target / goto_target /
# note_head_command / tool_move_head with timestamp + thread + pose.
# Empty = no logging (no overhead). External logrotate recommended; the
# logger appends without size cap.
MOTOR_LOG_PATH=

# ── Elder-care mode (P6/P7/P8) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Master gate. When OFF (0/false/no/off/unset), every elder-care helper is
# a no-op and production behaviour is byte-for-byte unchanged. Turn ON to
# enable: pre-LLM emergency-phrase route, TTS rate -10%, +400 ms inter-turn
# pause, and antenna "listening" cue on VAD edge.
ELDER_CARE_MODE=0

# Optional HTTPS endpoint that receives a JSON POST when an emergency phrase
# is detected (救命 / fall / chest pain / call my daughter / 護士 ...). Payload:
# {"ts": float, "phrase": str, "text": str, "robot": "reachy-mini"}.
# Empty = log-only (always written to /home/pollen/brain/logs/emergency.log).
ELDER_EMERGENCY_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Extra silence (milliseconds) appended after TTS_TAIL_DRAIN_S when elder
# mode is on. Research (PMC10917141) recommends ~400 ms extra inter-turn
# gap for elderly conversation partners.
ELDER_PAUSE_MS=400

# Antenna forward-dip magnitude (radians) for the listening cue. Clamped
# to [0.0, 0.5]. 0.15 rad ≈ 8.6° — visible but not theatrical.
ELDER_ANTENNA_DIP_RAD=0.15

# ── Wave4-P4 ElderFallGuard (MediaPipe Pose fall detector, #74) ───────
# OFF by default. When enabled, brain spawns a fall-detection worker that
# subscribes to the existing tracking_loop camera frame (no new camera
# open — respects Wave3-P2 single-owner invariant) and runs MediaPipe Pose
# at ~3 Hz. Triggers elder_care.log_emergency + post_webhook on a confirmed
# fall (phrase="fall_detected"), reusing the existing webhook signature.
# Production must NOT enable without explicit human review of false-positive
# rate (#77 soak gate). Thresholds adapted from arXiv 2505.11845.
ELDER_FALLGUARD_ENABLED=0
ELDER_FALLGUARD_MODEL=/home/pollen/brain/models/pose_landmarker_lite.task
ELDER_FALLGUARD_HZ=3                   # detection rate (1-10 Hz)
ELDER_FALLGUARD_PRONE_S=3.0            # paper: prone pose held > 3 s
ELDER_FALLGUARD_GRACE_S=10.0           # grace window before alert
ELDER_FALLGUARD_COOLDOWN_S=60.0        # min seconds between repeat alerts
ELDER_FALLGUARD_RECREATE_S=300         # PoseLandmarker recreate (leak mitigation)
# H-F1: prone-only entry into SUSPECT requires the subject to have been
# seen upright within this many seconds. Defeats already-lying false
# positives (sleeping on sofa, child on floor, tilted camera, short user)
# at the cost of missing falls from a never-seen-upright subject — an
# acceptable trade for an opt-in monitoring aide (not a first responder).
ELDER_FALLGUARD_GRACE_UPRIGHT_S=60.0
# H-F2: dead-letter queue for fall webhooks that fail all 3 retry
# attempts. A future reconciler can replay these JSONL lines. Default
# under $HOME/brain so it follows the systemd --user WorkingDirectory.
# ELDER_FALLGUARD_WEBHOOK_DLQ=/home/pollen/brain/.webhook_dlq.jsonl

# ── MediaPipe HandLandmarker — REMOVED Wave6-P2 #94 ───────────────────
# HAND_LANDMARKER_ENABLED + HAND_LANDMARKER_RECREATE_S env vars and the
# hand_worker thread / count_fingers_in_frame() code path were deleted
# entirely (commit Wave6-P2 #94) to permanently eliminate the aarch64
# MediaPipe IMAGE-mode leak (mediapipe#5217 / #4785) that auto-restarted
# the Pi brain every ~16 min. If still in your existing .env, both vars
# are now ignored — safe to remove. MediaPipe remains a project dep for
# elder_fallguard.py (PoseLandmarker, separate module).

# ── GStreamer (WebRTC) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Path to Pollen's Rust plugins (gst-plugins-rs) if not in system path.
# GST_PLUGIN_PATH=/opt/gst-plugins-rs/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu

# ── Observability (D2-OBS-BRAIN) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Prometheus /metrics exporter (prometheus_client.start_http_server).
# Bind 0.0.0.0 so Grafana / Prometheus running on s1 / a remote host can
# scrape; firewall the port at the network layer if exposed beyond LAN.
BRAIN_PROMETHEUS_PORT=9101
BRAIN_PROMETHEUS_ADDR=0.0.0.0
# Per-thread heartbeat watchdog: every INTERVAL_S the watchdog thread
# inspects the OLDEST registered heartbeat. If older than THRESHOLD_S the
# WATCHDOG=1 sd_notify is SKIPPED so systemd's WatchdogSec (=120 in the
# production unit) trips and the unit restarts. Catches GStreamer /
# gupnp-spin starvation that the old unconditional idle-loop pulse missed.
# Default 90 s (raised from 60 s 2026-05-29 after H-O4 review). The slowest
# legitimate worker call is vision_worker's VL HTTP to vllm0528 which can take
# 30-60 s under load; a 60 s ceiling would mark a healthy worker stale
# mid-call, then the OS kill cycle would mask the real backend slowdown.
BRAIN_WATCHDOG_THRESHOLD_S=90
BRAIN_WATCHDOG_INTERVAL_S=10
# Spoken when vLLM fails or its circuit is open. Defaults to "嗯…我想想。"
# (zh-TW). Override for English-first deployments — keep it short (<=12 chars)
# so the user perceives a "thinking" beat rather than a stall.
# BRAIN_LLM_FALLBACK_PHRASE=嗯…我想想。

# ── Wave4-P11 #85 gupnp-igd-thread CPU cap (Option C symptom mitigation) ──
# libgupnp-igd-1.6's GMainLoop worker (comm `gupnp-igd-threa`, truncated) busy-
# spins to 33-43% CPU within ~5 min when no IGD is reachable (always the case
# on Tailscale userspace). The brain spawns an in-process sidecar that re-
# discovers the gupnp TIDs every BRAIN_GUPNP_CAP_INTERVAL seconds and drops
# them to SCHED_IDLE + pinned to BRAIN_GUPNP_CAP_CORE. Default ON (symptom
# relief is free on Linux; gracefully no-ops on non-Linux). Pi 4 systemd user
# unit pins brain to AllowedCPUs=2,3 — keep CAP_CORE inside that set (3).
BRAIN_GUPNP_CAP_ENABLED=1
BRAIN_GUPNP_CAP_CORE=3
BRAIN_GUPNP_CAP_INTERVAL=30

# ── Wave4-P3 #73 Option B — cooperative motion abort (barge-in) ──
# When user speech is detected mid-action (nod/shake/happy/think/greet/
# look_around), src/motion_abort.py's module-global threading.Event is
# set, and the running do_action's inter-step interruptible_sleep wakes
# within ~50 ms so the robot stops moving and starts listening. No env
# knobs — the 50 ms polling interval is hard-coded in src/motion_abort.py
# because tuning it does not move real-world UX (human reaction-time
# floor ≈ 200 ms). Prometheus: brain_motion_abort_total{reason}.
# structlog events: motion_abort_requested / motion_aborted_at_step.
# Original 3-layer priority-queue spec was over-engineered for the
# single-user elder-care scenario; this minimal Event-based path
# replaces it (verdict #92 RESTART_FRESH).
